5.0     Major Release - Modern Web UI & Security

    BREAKING CHANGES
    * Remove legacy form-urlencoded POST command API
      - External scripts using commands like `command=restart&camid=1` will break
      - Migrate to new JSON REST API endpoints (see API CHANGES below)

    API CHANGES
    * Replace legacy POST commands with JSON REST API endpoints:
      - POST /0/api/config/write (replaces command=config_write)
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/restart (replaces command=restart)
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/snapshot (replaces command=snapshot)
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/pause with {"action":"on|off|schedule"}
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/stop (replaces command=stop)
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/event/start (replaces command=eventstart)
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/event/end (replaces command=eventend)
      - POST /{camId}/api/camera/ptz with {"action":"pan_left|pan_right|..."}
    * All new endpoints require X-CSRF-Token header for CSRF protection
    * All new endpoints return JSON responses: {"status":"ok"} or {"error":"..."}

    PLATFORM REQUIREMENTS
    * Raspberry Pi 4 or newer required (64-bit only)
    * Raspberry Pi 3 and older NOT supported due to:
      - libcamera API changes requiring newer GPU firmware
      - 64-bit OS requirement (armhf/32-bit deprecated)
      - Insufficient RAM for bcrypt + multi-camera workloads
    * Tested platforms: Raspberry Pi 4, Raspberry Pi 5

    AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY
    * Implement bcrypt password hashing with work factor 12 (webu_auth.hpp/cpp)
    * Add CLI setup tool for password configuration (motion-setup binary)
    * Support --reset flag for password recovery
    * Support --config flag for alternate config file paths
    * Add auto-detection of bcrypt vs plaintext passwords (backward compatible)
    * Add auto-hashing for password changes via Settings UI
    * Fix admin username to "admin" to prevent username enumeration attacks
    * Add CSRF protection with per-session tokens
    * Add session-based authentication with 64-char cryptographic tokens
    * Add configurable session timeout (webcontrol_session_timeout parameter)
    * Add sliding window session expiration
    * Log warnings when plaintext passwords detected

    WEB UI (React)
    * Complete React 18 + TypeScript + Vite web interface
    * Implement AuthGate component for protected routes
    * Implement LoginPage with session management
    * Add Settings page with readonly admin username field
    * Implement live camera streaming via MJPEG
    * Add thumbnail display for folder-based media browsing
    * Implement snapshot button for manual image capture
    * Add folder-based media browsing with delete-all functionality

    RASPBERRY PI 5 SUPPORT
    * Raspberry Pi 5 + Camera Module v3 (IMX708) native support
    * Change libcamera StreamRole from Viewfinder to VideoRecording for Pi 5 PiSP
    * Add multi-buffer support for libcamera with configurable buffer count
    * Add camera filtering to exclude USB cameras from CSI camera detection
    * Add model-based camera selection for libcamera devices
    * Add libcam_buffer_count configuration parameter (default: 4)

    CONFIGURATION SYSTEM REFACTOR
    * Major configuration system refactor for improved performance
    * Add O(1) parameter registry with hash map lookup (parm_registry.hpp/cpp)
    * Add scoped parameter structs for reduced memory footprint (parm_structs.hpp)
    * Add O(1) scoped copy operations (copy_app, copy_cam, copy_snd)
    * Separate file I/O from configuration storage (conf_file.hpp/cpp)
    * Replace linear array iteration with registry-based lookups in conf.cpp
    * Integrate O(1) registry lookups into edit_set_active() and parms_copy()
    * Add movie_encoder_preset config parameter for H.264 encoding

    BUILD SYSTEM
    * Add libxcrypt detection in configure.ac for bcrypt support
    * Add motion-setup to bin_PROGRAMS in Makefile.am
    * Add webu_auth.cpp/hpp to motion_SOURCES

    BUG FIXES
    * Fix deadlock in check_restart() — second pthread_mutex_lock should be
      pthread_mutex_unlock; database config restart permanently deadlocked
      the main application thread (motion.cpp)
    * Fix null pointer dereference in passthru_check() — nullptr guard was
      placed after the pointer dereference, causing potential SEGV during
      netcam disconnect/reconnect (movie.cpp)
    * Fix buffer underflow in ff_log() — strlen(buff)-1 wraps to SIZE_MAX
      when FFmpeg emits an empty log message, causing out-of-bounds write
      (logger.cpp)
    * Fix schedule time-range comparison — independent hour/minute inequalities
      failed for virtually all practical schedule windows; replaced with
      linearized total-minutes comparison (schedule.cpp)
    * Fix HammingWindow formula — incorrect parentheses produced a flat
      constant (~0.54) for all samples instead of a smooth taper (sound.cpp)
    * Fix HannWindow formula — multiplication instead of division zeroed all
      input samples, completely disabling sound detection for Hann window
      users (sound.cpp)
    * Fix movie_retain config parameter silently ignored — missing handler in
      dispatch_edit() caused the value to be discarded; "secondary" retention
      mode had no effect (conf.cpp)
    * Fix PostgreSQL connection string injection — single quotes and backslashes
      in database credentials broke PQconnectdb() connection string (dbse.cpp)
    * Fix out-of-bounds array access in text overlay — non-ASCII characters in
      text_left/text_right caused undefined behavior via negative or >126 index
      into char_arr_ptr[127] (draw.cpp)
    * Fix JSON parser rejecting valid \uXXXX unicode escape sequences — added
      full RFC 8259 compliant handler with UTF-8 encoding and surrogate pair
      support (json_parse.cpp)
    * Fix log history vector growing unbounded on counter overflow — reinit
      appended 200 entries without clearing existing ones (logger.cpp)
    * Fix potential 1-byte buffer overflow in write_norm() — newline append
      could write past msg_full[1024] when SHOW_ERRNO filled buffer to capacity
      (logger.cpp)
    * Fix uninitialized retcd in passthru_streams() — non-video/non-audio stream
      types caused undefined behavior on first loop iteration (movie.cpp)
    * Fix cleandir running every 30 seconds with unknown freq value — missing
      else clause left next_ts unchanged; now defaults to daily with warning
      (schedule.cpp)
    * Fix ALSA hw_params and PCM handle leak — 10 error paths after
      snd_pcm_hw_params_malloc returned without freeing resources; converted to
      goto-cleanup pattern (sound.cpp)
    * Fix thumbnail false success reporting — encode/write failures after
      sws_scale left retcd positive, causing "Generated thumbnail" log for
      broken files (thumbnail.cpp)
    * Fix partial thumbnail file permanently blocking regeneration — write
      failures left empty/partial file on disk; exists() check prevented retry;
      now removes partial files on failure (thumbnail.cpp)
    * Fix fd leak in vlp_open_vidpipe() — sysfs name file descriptor not closed
      on successful loopback pipe detection (video_loopback.cpp)
    * Fix fd leak in vlp_startpipe() — three ioctl error paths returned without
      closing the opened device fd (video_loopback.cpp)
    * Fix misleading CIDR support comment in is_trusted_proxy() — code only
      performs exact IP matching, not CIDR range matching (webu_ans.cpp)
    * Fix mutex held during external command execution in failauth_check() —
      lock script could stall all web connections; now releases mutex before
      exec (webu_ans.cpp)
    * Fix stream_max_connections config parameter unreachable — handler existed
      in dispatch_edit() but missing from config_parms[] array; users could not
      configure max concurrent stream connections (conf.cpp)
    * Fix CLOCK_MONOTONIC passed to localtime_r in database handler — produced
      meaningless wall-clock hours; cleanup ran at boot-relative intervals instead
      of aligned to real hours; changed to CLOCK_REALTIME (dbse.cpp)
    * Fix mysql_init() return value not checked — NULL return on library init
      failure would leave struct in indeterminate state before mysql_real_connect;
      added null check with error logging and cleanup (dbse.cpp)
    * Fix 'M' glyph bitmap missing 7th pixel in row 4 — only 6 values instead
      of 7; zero-initialized gap caused one-pixel cosmetic defect in text
      overlays (draw.cpp)
    * Remove 11 unreachable MOTION_LOG statements after return in config edit
      handlers — dead code from disabled debug traces (conf.cpp)
    * Remove dead float cast in allcam getsizes_scale — (float) applied to
      already-computed integer was a no-op (allcam.cpp)
    * Remove redundant duplicate assignment of out pointer in draw location() —
      variable initialized and immediately reassigned to same value (draw.cpp)
    * Remove duplicate #include "picture.hpp" (picture.cpp)
    * Remove 3 dead imgts self-assignments in process_preview() — pointer
      save/restore made the struct copies no-ops (picture.cpp)
    * Refactor stream_free()/stream_alloc() from magic-number if/else chains to
      range-for over pointer array — eliminates fragile hard-coded stream slot
      count (allcam.cpp)

